**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests`

**How to implement.** The product composition root imports the shipped catalogue before any window opens (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`, §3.4). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`, `AppContext.create (settings)`: it builds `CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()` and runs `stores.proxy.importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. An `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`, and the app starts with what was imported; nothing throws, as in `DefaultStores.create` (step 42). `materials`, `samples` and `categories` are the import's stores, `sources` is `Library.SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`, and `library` is `Library.liveLibrary stores.libraryEntries stores.samples sources`. Every other field and the signature are unchanged, so `Program.fs:59` (`Startup.context`, evaluated before `LauncherWindow` opens at `:216`) and every test composition keep their code. The `Lifecycle`, `MaterialStore` and `SampleStore` opens go. (2) The comments the switch makes false say what is true, in no more words: `create`'s doc (`AppContext.fs:69-77`, 'every app start re-seeds') says the stores start empty and are filled from the Built-in catalogue (spec 0050 §3.4); the `VersionsInUse` paragraph (`:79-87`) goes with the store construction it explained; and the `library` field's doc (`:27-29`) says the presets are imported. The self-seeding store docs drop 'the app composition root keeps calling this unchanged': `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` in `MaterialLibrary.fs`, `MaterialProxy.createInMemory` in `MaterialStore.fs` and `SampleProxy.createInMemory` in `SampleStore.fs` (`:183-185`). `liveLibrary`'s doc in `ElementId.fs` says that `presets` is the preset store, which the composition roots fill from the Built-in catalogue. `WireUiCompositionTests`' module doc says that `AppContext.create` fills empty stores from the Built-in catalogue. (3) Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores`: over `freshContext ()`, the samples, materials and categories list exactly `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`, `materials ()` and `categories ()` by id (`IncludeInactive` where the store takes a scope), and `library.tryGetEntry` resolves every `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()` entry to itself. `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create re-seeds its own` (`AppContextTests.fs:117-126`) becomes `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create imports its own`, with its body unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the wiring, `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT call `MaterialProxy.createInMemory`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory`, `CategoryProxy.createInMemory` or `Library.createInMemory`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including the WireUiCompositionTests and WireUi0040CompositionTests acceptance facts over the real `AppContext.create`; ui-tests MUST pass over AppContextTests, LauncherTests, TableAndElementRotationTests and WireUiFinalCompositionTests, including `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores` and `two separate app scopes do NOT share stores — each create imports its own`; and build, elevation and the six s06 invariants MUST pass.
